## At a glance

| Dimension | WhyLabs | Tracify |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Primary focus** | LLM model quality monitoring | Agent workflow observability |
| **Model drift** | Native (LLM-specific) | Limited |
| **Agent context** | Not native | Native |
| **Evaluation** | External integration | Integrated |
| **Cost tracking** | None | Comprehensive |
| **Multi-turn sessions** | Not native | Native |
| **Best for** | LLM teams | Agent product teams |

WhyLabs monitors LLM output quality; Tracify ensures agents achieve their goals.

## Core difference

**WhyLabs** is LLM-specific: monitors output toxicity, drift, hallucinations, quality degradation at the model level. **Tracify** is agent-specific: monitors multi-turn outcomes, cost, quality gates, experiments.

Choose WhyLabs for LLM monitoring; choose Tracify for agent observability.

## Scenario 1: monitoring LLM output quality

You want to detect when LLM outputs start containing toxic language, hallucinations, or drift from baseline.

**With WhyLabs:** Purpose-built LLM monitoring, toxicity detection, hallucination scoring, quality drift.

**With Tracify:** Generic quality evaluation. Less LLM-specialized.

**Result:** WhyLabs wins on LLM-specific signals.

## Scenario 2: multi-agent system

You have agents routing between models, handling multi-turn conversations, requiring cost optimization.

**With WhyLabs:** Model-level monitoring. Doesn't capture agent routing, session context, or cost.

**With Tracify:** Agent-level observability: sessions, cost breakdown, agent-specific evaluations.

**Result:** Tracify wins on agent-level context.

## Cost and setup

Both platforms are $1-2k/month at moderate scale. WhyLabs requires LLM-specific instrumentation; Tracify works with generic spans.

## When to choose each

**Choose WhyLabs:** If LLM-specific quality monitoring is critical (toxicity, hallucinations, etc.)
**Choose Tracify:** If agent outcomes and cost matter

